	],
	"abilities": [
		"Synth and drum sequencing",
		"USB MIDI",
		"DIN MIDI",
		"MIDI clock",
		"Configurable track channels",
		"Deep synth-engine CC editing on channels 1 and 2",
		"Per-drum sample, pitch, decay, distortion, EQ, pan and level CCs on channel 10",
		"Synth patch SysEx supported by protocol-aware editors"
	],
	"hardwareControls": [
		"32 pads",
		"Eight macro encoders",
		"Eight track buttons",
		"Master filter",
		"Master volume"
	],
	"notice": "Synths default to MIDI channels 1 and 2, external MIDI tracks to 3 and 4, and all four drum tracks to 10. Connect USB MIDI or the 5-pin MIDI ports. Hold Shift and press Save for Setup View to configure channels and independently enable note, CC, program-change and clock transmission/receive. Channel 16 is reserved for project selection. Pad notes and encoder behavior depend on the current view and configuration; this profile supplies setup guidance and an unbound physical surface, with no guessed CC or pad maps. USB port aliases have not been verified; select this profile manually. Diagrams are original schematics with illustrative positions, not scaled hardware drawings. The CC controls use factory channels 1/2 for synths and 10 for drums; remap after hardware channel changes. The two MIDI tracks default to channels 3/4. NRPN, full patch dumps, project file transfer, acknowledgements, pacing and checksums require the linked library or another protocol-aware host; they are not modeled as single CCs. The community project-transfer protocol is independently reverse-engineered. Parameter changes from the generic controls list are remote sound editing, not extra physical knobs.",
